WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.090
On 27 September 2022,
Hurricane Ian hit western Cuba,

2
00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:06.970
in Pinar del Río.

3
00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:10.110
The next day, it hit south-west Florida.

4
00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:15.150
Ian caused 112.9 billion
dollars of damage in the US.

5
00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.930
Cuba recorded 5 deaths, 3 of them direct.

6
00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:24.690
In Florida, there were 66 direct
deaths, and the US had 90 more indirect.

7
00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:27.510
The US is far richer than Cuba.

8
00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:30.930
So why did far more people die in Florida?

9
00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:34.410
In this mission, you'll sort Ian's
primary and secondary effects,

10
00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:36.990
in Florida and in Cuba.

11
00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:39.330
Then you'll compare how
each country responded,

12
00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:43.030
in the first days and
over the years after.

13
00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:48.040
Your mission: explain why far more
people died in Florida than in Cuba.
